
<p>Every to-do list runs forever. Ivy runs for a day. Each morning you turn ideas into a plan. Each evening, whatever’s left is an idea again. Nothing is overdue. Tomorrow starts empty.</p>

<p>I’m <a href="https://www.t3rtium.net">Jürgen Schweizer</a>, founder of Semantical. I spent years building a to-do app and never expected to build another. Then I came across the Ivy Lee Method. We built a prototype and couldn’t stop using it.</p>

<p>Beneath the calm: Calendar and Reminders integration, focus sessions, Screen Time shields, and a daily journal. All native: SwiftUI, UIKit, Metal.</p>

<p><a href="https://apps.apple.com/app/apple-store/id6747921058?pt=1363339&amp;ct=Daring-Fireball-Post&amp;mt=8">Ivy is on iPhone</a>, with Mac to follow. <a href="mailto:hello@semantical.com">Let me know</a> what you think!</p>

